:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal/country"} "Medals by country"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal/athlete"} "Medals by athlete"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/medal_table"} "Medal tables"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/participation"} "Participations"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/records"} "Olympic Records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age"} "Age records"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics/age_at_death"} "Age at death"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/lists"} "Lists"]] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/today"} "Today"]] "\n" [:li {}] "\n" [:li {:class "divider"}] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/statistics"} "Statistics"]] "\n"] "\n"] "\n\n\n\n\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/feedbacks/new"} "Feedback"]] "\n" [:form {:class "navbar-form navbar-left", :role "search", :action "/athletes/quick_search", :accept-charset "UTF-8", :method "post"} [:input {:name "utf8", :type "hidden", :value "✓", :autocomplete "off"}] [:input {:type "hidden", :name "authenticity_token", :value "7Q5hcB4T116fjnZew0lxyamG5cetXo8jtKdO-mQQnLgu7Od-mG-SQMhIRhl_k1SKshd2cI4Cn1XSDVayvEoG8g", :autocomplete "off"}] [:div {:class "form-group"} "\n" [:input {:type "text", :name "query", :id "query", :class "form-control", :placeholder "Athlete search"}] "\n"] "\n" [:input {:type "submit", :name "commit", :value "Go", :class "btn btn-default", :data-disable-with "Go"}] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "container"} "\n" [:ol {:class "breadcrumb"} "\n" [:li {} "\n" [:a {:href "/"} "Home"] "\n"] "\n" [:li {} [:a {:href "/editions"} "Games"]] [:li {:class "active"} "1994 Winter Olympics Overview"] "\n"] "\n\n\n" [:h1 {} "1994 Winter Olympics"] "\n" [:h2 {} "Facts"] "\n" [:table {:class "biotable"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Competition type"] "\n" [:td {} "Olympic Games"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Number and Year"] "\n" [:td {} "XVII / 1994"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Host city"] "\n" [:td {} "\nLillehammer, Norway\n(" [:a {:href "/venues/editions/45"} "Venues"] ")\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Opening ceremony"] "\n" [:td {} "\n12 February\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Closing ceremony"] "\n" [:td {} "\n27 February\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Competition dates"] "\n" [:td {} "\n12 – 27 February\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "OCOG"] "\n" [:td {} [:a {:href "/organizations/319"} "Lillehammer Olympic Organizing Committee"]] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Participants"] "\n" [:td {} "\n" [:a {:href "/counts/edition/45"} "1738"] "\nfrom " [:a {:href "/editions/45/countries"} "67 countries"] "\n"] "\n"] "\n" [:tr {} "\n" [:th {} "Medal events"] "\n" [:td {} "\n61\nin 12 disciplines\n"] "\n"] "\n"]] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "\nOverview\n\n"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Before the Lillehammer Olympics began, they were haunted by tragedy and controversy. There was the " [:a {:href "/athletes/81471"} "Nancy Kerrigan"] "-" [:a {:href "/athletes/81251"} "Tonya Harding"] " story, in which Harding’s bodyguard and ex-husband admitted to attacking Kerrigan prior to the U.S. Olympic Trials, a story which was ubiquitous in the U.S. press and television. Two weeks before the Olympics, skiing medal favorite " [:a {:href "/athletes/81746"} "Ulrike Maier"] " of Austria was killed when she fell and broke her neck in a downhill race. U.S. ice dancer " [:a {:href "/athletes/82136"} "Elizabeth Punsalan"] "’s father was savagely stabbed to death one week before the Olympics; allegedly by his son, Elizabeth’s brother. For the Norwegians, they were stunned in October 1993 when their greatest sporting hero, " [:a {:href "/athletes/98479"} "Vegard Ulvang"] ", tragically lost his brother " [:a {:href "/athletes/900820"} "Kjetil"] ", who died in the Arctic wilderness while skiing. They also had to deal with the death of the Norwegian ski coach in December 1993. Finally, only days before the Games, " [:a {:href "/athletes/85701"} "Ole Gunnar Fidjestøl"] ", the Norwegian ski jumper who was to ski jump the torch into the stadium at the opening ceremonies, crashed during a practice jump, sustaining a concussion. He had to be replaced by his understudy, Stein Gruben. Lillehammer seemed to be cursed."] "\n\n" [:p {} "And tragically, Lillehammer was haunted by the recent news from its sister Olympic Winter city of a decade ago, Sarajevo. Sarajevo, which had hosted a beautiful " [:a {:href "/editions/42"} "Olympic Winter Games in 1984"] ", now lay in ruins, its stadia and people destroyed by a senseless war in which the Serbs attempted an “ethnic cleansing” on Bosnia-Herzegovina, killing many of their former Muslim brethren."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Stein Gruben performed beautifully at the Opening Ceremony, as did all of Norway. The Ceremonies began a mystical two weeks which ended all thoughts of the tragedy and controversy which had preceded them, and reminded us again of what the Olympics and sport can bring to the world. The Olympic Winter Games had gone from the ridiculous to the sublime."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were many great athletic feats at the Lillehammer Games. " [:a {:href "/athletes/80945"} "Manuela Di Centa"] " won five medals in cross-country skiing. Norway’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/88548"} "Johann Olav Koss"] " won three speed skating gold medals in world record time. " [:a {:href "/athletes/87473"} "Dan Jansen"] " won the hearts of sports fans everywhere when he finally won a gold medal in the " [:a {:href "/results/1085"} "1,000 metre speed skating"] ". But through it all, the champions seemed to be the small town of Lillehammer and the people of Norway itself."] "\n\n" [:p {} "There were also many poignant memories of Sarajevo. " [:a {:href "/athletes/83053"} "Katarina Witt"] " skated her long program to “Where Have All the Flowers Gone?” in memory of the citizens who had lost their lives in that senseless war. On the next-to-last night, at the figure skating exhibition, " [:a {:href "/athletes/82881"} "Jayne Torvill"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/85109"} "Christopher Dean"] " skated “Bolero” as they had done so hauntingly in 1984. Koss donated a major portion of his Olympic bonus (about $33,000) to Olympic Aid for the citizens of Sarajevo. And during the Lillehammer Olympics, President " [:a {:href "/athletes/899318"} "Samaranch"] " visited Sarajevo, seeing in person the stark contrast between the Olympic City and the Sarajevo of 1994. At the Closing Ceremony, Samaranch also spoke movingly about Sarajevo."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In summing up the Lillehammer Olympics, Leigh Montville of " [:em {} "Sports Illustrated"] " said it best, “The XVII Winter Olympics did not exist. Norway did not exist. These were the fairy-tale Games, drawn from the imagination, staged in the pages of a children’s book. They could not exist. Reality cannot be this good.”"] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Bid process"] "\n" [:div {:class "description"} "\n" [:p {} "Bid voting at the 94th " [:a {:href "/meetings"} "IOC Session"] " in Seoul on 15 September 1988."] "\n\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped"} "\n  \t" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:th {}] "\n  \t\t" [:th {}] "\n  \t\t" [:th {} "Round 1"] "\n  \t\t" [:th {} "Round 2"] "\n  \t\t" [:th {} "Round 3"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Lillehammer"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Norway"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "25"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "30"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "45"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Östersund"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Sweden"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "19"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "33"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "39"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Anchorage, Alaska"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "United States"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "23"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "22"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "–"] "\n  \t"] [:tr {} "\n  \t\t" [:td {:class "city"} "Sofia"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "Bulgaria"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "17"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "–"] "\n  \t\t" [:td {} "–"] "\n  "]]] "\n\n"] "\n\n" [:h2 {} "Ceremonies"] "\n" [:table {:class "table table-striped table-condensed"} "\n" [:tbody {} [:tr {} "\n" [:th